  "term": "probability sampling",
  "definition": "Probability sampling is a sampling approach commonly used in quantitative research, contrasted with purposive sampling in qualitative work. Rather than choosing participants because they are especially informative about a topic, it relies on selection by probability-based methods such as random sampling.",
